 "text": "..title\nAn ordinance authorizing The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County to abandon existing public water main, fire hydrant assembly and easements, and to accept new public water main, fire hydrant assembly and easements, for property located at 222 25th Avenue North, also known as Centennial Sportsplex (MWS Project No. 26-WL-45 and Proposal No. 2026M071ES-001).\n..body\nWHEREAS, the abandonment of approximately 312 linear feet of existing six-inch water main, one fire hydrant assembly and easements, and the acceptance of approximately 587 linear feet of new six-inch water main (DIP), one new fire hydrant assembly and easements, for property located at 222 25th Avenue North, also known as Centennial Sportsplex, are needed to construct project number 26-WL-45; and,\nWHEREAS, the Metropolitan Planning Commission approved mandatory referral No. 2026M071ES-001 on August 17, 2026, for the abandonment and acceptance of said water mains, fire hydrant assemblies and easements.\nNOW, THEREFORE, BE IT ENACTED BY THE COUNCIL OF THE METROPOLITAN GOVERNMENT OF NASHVILLE AND DAVIDSON COUNTY:\nSection 1.\tThe Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County is authorized to abandon approximately 312 linear feet of existing six-inch water main, one fire hydrant assembly and easements, and to accept approximately 587 linear feet of new six-inch water main (DIP), one new fire hydrant assembly and easements, for property located at 222 25th Avenue North, also known as Centennial Sportsplex, as shown on Exhibit 1, which is attached hereto and incorporated by reference.\nMap & Parcel: \t\t\t\tAddress:\n09215003300\t\t\t\t\t222 25th Avenue North\nSection 2.\tThe Directors of Water and Sewerage Services and Public Property Administration are authorized to execute such documents as may be necessary and appropriate to carry out the abandonment and acceptance authorized by this ordinance. \nSection 3.\tAmendments to this legislation shall be approved by resolution.\nSection 4.\tThis ordinance shall take effect from and after its final passage, the welfare of The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County requiring it.\n..Agenda Analysis\nAnalysis\n\nThis ordinance abandons approximately 312 linear feet of existing six-inch water main, one fire hydrant assembly and easements, and accepts approximately 587 linear feet of new six-inch water main (DIP), one new fire hydrant assembly and easements, for property located at 222 25th Avenue North, also known as Centennial Sportsplex.\n\nFuture amendments to this legislation may be approved by resolution. This ordinance has been approved by the Planning Commission.\n\nFiscal Note: This ordinance has no cost to Metro. Abandoned easements have no market value according to the Department of Water and Sewerage Services.\n\n"
}
